hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
1237,"Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Keep your children close to you until the early part of the evening passes. That is the time when the devils spread out.\"""""
1238,"'Say farewell to Salma if you prepare to go in the morning,\n White hair and Islam is enough prohibition for a man'\n\n'Umar said, 'Enough! You have spoken the truth. You have spoken the truth.'\""1239""","As-Sa'ib ibn Yazid said, \'Umar", may Allah be pleased with him,\nused to pass by us in the middle of the day - or near to it - and\nsay," 'Get up and take a midday nap. Any time spent here after this is for\nshaytan.'\"""""
1240,"Anas said, \At the time that wine was made unlawful", there was\nno drink that the people of Madina liked better than that made from dried\ndates and unripe dates. I used to give the drink to the Companions of the\nMessenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace. They were\nin the home of Abu Talha when a man passed by and announced, 'Wine has\nbeen forbidden.' They did not say, 'When?' or 'Wait until we see.' They\nsaid, 'Anas, break them!' Then they said in the presence of Umm Sulaym,\n'Wait until it becomes cool and we have washed ourselves.' Then Umm Sulaym\nput perfume on them. Then they went to the Prophet, may Allah bless him\nand grant him peace," and the news was as the man had said.\"""""
1241,"Here is the translated text in English:

Musa narrated to us, saying: Sulaiman bin al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Thabit, who said: I, Anas, said: The people of Medina did not have a drink, after the prohibition of wine, as astonishing as the date and the grape. So, I would pour the drink for the companions of the Messenger of Allah, and they were at Abu Talhah's. A man got up and said: Wine has been prohibited. What did they say? ""When?"" or ""Until we see?"" They said: ""O Anas, pour it out!"" Then they went to Umm Sulaim's, until they had washed and purified themselves, and then Umm Sulaim poured water over them, and then they went to the Prophet, and the report was as the man had said. I, Anas, said: What did they eat after that?", there was\nno drink that the people of Madina liked better than that made from dried\ndates and unripe dates. I used to give the drink to the Companions of the\nMessenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace. They were\nin the home of Abu Talha when a man passed by and announced, 'Wine has\nbeen forbidden.' They did not say, 'When?' or 'Wait until we see.' They\nsaid, 'Anas, break them!' Then they said in the presence of Umm Sulaym,\n'Wait until it becomes cool and we have washed ourselves.' Then Umm Sulaym\nput perfume on them. Then they went to the Prophet, may Allah bless him\nand grant him peace," and the news was as the man had said.\"""""
1242,"Khawwat ibn Jubayr said, \Sleep at the beginning of the day is stupidity", in the middle of it is (an act of) character,"and at the end of it is imbecility.\"""""
